Subject: d3d9: Use the destination slice pitch for promoted volume uploads.

The software 16-bit texture promotion path advances each depth slice by one
row instead of one whole slice. For volume textures with height greater than
one, later slices overwrite earlier rows and leave the rest uninitialized.
Use the already computed destination slice pitch for the depth offset.

Based on d9vk f229921c1b7f14edeadeccff04a9e65d0a016148.
Regression: tests/d3d9-formats.c uploads a 4x3x3 A4R4G4B4 volume with distinct
slice colors, then samples each slice through fixed-function D3D9 rendering.

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -4972,7 +4972,7 @@
               + (SrcOffset.x) * 2);
             uint32_t* dstRow = reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(
               reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*>(slice.mapPtr)
-              + z * dstPitch
+              + z * dstSlicePitch
               + y * dstPitch);
 
             for (uint32_t x = 0; x < SrcExtent.width; x++) {
